Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:47:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/38] fs: sharedfs: read-only file system over the host index

Mount with: mount -t sharedfs none /mnt. The superblock takes the
session of the bound virtio device. Lookups, directory listings and
attributes come straight from the shared-memory index, read with the
host's per-entry seqlock. Dentries revalidate against the index by slot
and generation, refreshing inode attributes on the way, so host-side
changes to names and sizes show up on the next path walk. File data,
symlink targets and statfs go over the request virtqueue; a READ
scatters into the folio's page. The vring is only touched under a mutex
in process context: the virtqueue callback schedules a work item that
drains completions.

